From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: publish the BTM Response as wifi.sta btm-resp
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

Second half of the defect fixed by 922, for the other event that never
reached map-agent: the BSS Transition Management Response. Steering works,
but the controller is never told a client answered, so btm_success stays 0
and no policy can ever learn whether a steer succeeded.

Same root cause: libwifi asks hostapd for raw action frames - which is where
a BTM Response arrives - through the iopsys-only ubus method event_mask_add,
which OpenWrt's hostapd does not have. The subscription fails with "Method
not found" and the frame never arrives. map-agent's own handler
(process_sta_btm_resp_evt) and everything below it, down to
wifi_send_sta_report(), have always been correct and simply never fire.

hostapd does emit the response on the control interface of the hapd that
received it:

  BSS-TM-RESP <addr> status_code=<u> bss_termination_delay=<u> [target_bssid=<mac>]

so it lands on the affiliated link's socket, which this source already holds
and drains. Publish it from there.

Details that are easy to get wrong and were checked against the consumer:

  - map-agent parses "status" as a STRING, not an integer.
  - "target_bssid" is absent when the client rejected the request; the
    handler treats it as optional and only reads it on success.
  - the address is translated to the affiliated one through the table 922
    fills on association, so a client is named identically in both events.
    Without that, agent_get_sta() misses on an MLO client.
  - "bssid" carries the link the response arrived on. map-agent resolves the
    AP for this event by ifname, and an affiliated link has no name it knows
    (it holds wlan0/1/2 and ap-mld-1/2, never ap-mld-1_link2), so the event
    is published under the parent name and patch 99996 makes map-agent
    prefer the BSSID - the same resolution its association path uses.

This patch alone does not make btm_success move: hostapd discards every BTM
Response unless bss_transition=1 is in its config, which OpenWrt defaults to
0 and nothing here was setting ("Ignore BSS Transition Management Response
... since BSS Transition Management is disabled", measured on bpi-4g). That
is handled outside this feed by the wnm-enable service.

Applies on top of 922-hostapd-ctrl-publishes-wifi-sta.patch and reuses its
helpers. Touches only the hapdctrl source in libwifi/modules/wpactrl/wpactrl.c.

--- a/libwifi/modules/wpactrl/wpactrl.c	2026-08-04 14:51:50.109595855 +0200
+++ b/libwifi/modules/wpactrl/wpactrl.c	2026-08-04 14:51:50.109637785 +0200
@@ -1026,8 +1026,83 @@
 	w->req.cb(&w->req);
 }
 
+/* Publish a BTM Response as the ubus "wifi.sta" event "btm-resp" (923).
+ *
+ * hostapd emits this on the control interface of the hapd the response arrived
+ * on - an affiliated link on an MLD:
+ *
+ *   BSS-TM-RESP <addr> status_code=<u> bss_termination_delay=<u> [target_bssid=<mac>]
+ *
+ * map-agent already handles the event end to end: process_sta_btm_resp_evt()
+ * parses it and calls wifi_send_sta_report(), which is what makes btm_success
+ * move at all. Nothing was ever publishing it, for the same reason nothing
+ * published an association - libwifi asks for raw action frames through the
+ * iopsys-only hostapd ubus method event_mask_add, which OpenWrt's hostapd does
+ * not have, so the subscription fails and the frame never arrives.
+ *
+ * NOTE map-agent parses "status" as a STRING, not an integer.
+ *
+ * The address is translated to the affiliated one through the same table the
+ * association path fills, so a client is named identically in both events;
+ * otherwise agent_get_sta() would miss on an MLO client.
+ *
+ * "bssid" carries the link this arrived on. map-agent resolves the AP for this
+ * event by ifname, which cannot name an affiliated link, so patch 99996 lets it
+ * prefer the BSSID - the resolution its association path already uses.
+ */
+static void hapdctrl_emit_btm_resp(struct hapdctrl_event *w,
+				   struct hapdctrl_sock *s, const char *msg)
+{
+	struct event_response *resp = &w->req.resp;
+	uint8_t mac[6], aff[6], target[6];
+	const uint8_t *sta = mac;
+	char tgt[64] = {0};
+	const char *p;
+	int status, len;
+
+	if (!w->req.cb || !resp->data || resp->maxlen < 2)
+		return;
+
+	if (hapdctrl_event_mac(msg, "BSS-TM-RESP", mac) != 0)
+		return;
+
+	p = strstr(msg, "status_code=");
+	if (!p)
+		return;
+	status = atoi(p + strlen("status_code="));
+
+	if (hapdctrl_sock_info(s))
+		return;
+
+	if (s->link_id >= 0 && hapdctrl_stamap_get(s, mac, aff, false) == 0)
+		sta = aff;
+
+	/* Absent when the client rejected the request; map-agent treats the
+	 * field as optional and only reads it on success. */
+	p = strstr(msg, "target_bssid=");
+	if (p && hwaddr_aton(p + strlen("target_bssid="), target))
+		snprintf(tgt, sizeof(tgt),
+			 ", \"target_bssid\":\"" HAPD_MACFMT "\"",
+			 HAPD_MACARG(target));
+
+	len = snprintf((char *)resp->data, resp->maxlen,
+		       "wifi.sta '{\"ifname\":\"%s\", \"event\":\"btm-resp\""
+		       ", \"data\":{\"macaddr\":\"" HAPD_MACFMT "\""
+		       ", \"status\":\"%d\"%s"
+		       ", \"bssid\":\"" HAPD_MACFMT "\"}}'",
+		       w->key, HAPD_MACARG(sta), status, tgt,
+		       HAPD_MACARG(s->bssid));
+
+	if (len < 0 || (uint32_t)len >= resp->maxlen)
+		return;		/* truncated: publishing half a MAC would lie */
+
+	resp->type = WIFI_EVENT_STA_ASSOC;
+	resp->len = len;
+	w->req.cb(&w->req);
+}
+
 /* Parse one hostapd control message: mutate the parent cache (atomic RMW) and
- * publish client association changes (922). */
+ * publish client association changes (922) and BTM responses (923). */
 static void hapdctrl_parse_event(struct hapdctrl_event *w,
 				 struct hapdctrl_sock *s, const char *msg)
 {
@@ -1051,6 +1126,8 @@
 			apconn_cache_sta_del(key, mac);
 			hapdctrl_emit_sta(w, s, mac, false);
 		}
+	} else if (strstr(msg, "BSS-TM-RESP")) {
+		hapdctrl_emit_btm_resp(w, s, msg);
 	} else if (strstr(msg, "AP-ENABLED")) {
 		struct hapdctrl_ev ev = { .set_enabled = true, .enabled = true };
 
